# Valgavoth, Terror Eater: "If a card you didn't control would be put into an opponent's graveyard from anywhere, exile it
# instead" (CR 614.1a), and "During your turn, you may play cards exiled with Valgavoth. If you cast a spell this way, pay
# life equal to its mana value rather than pay its mana cost" (CR 607.2b, 305.1, 118.9, 119.4).
# Bot1 casts Valgavoth off three Black Lotuses, which go to Bot1's own graveyard (not an opponent's). On turn 2 Bot2 loses
# cards from every zone: its Black Lotus sacrificed from the battlefield, Faithless Looting and Lightning Bolt resolving off
# the stack, a Mountain and an Island discarded from its hand; each is exiled with Valgavoth. Bot1 can't cast the Bolt on
# Bot2's turn. On turn 3, Bot1's, Bot1 plays the Mountain from exile as its land play, casts the Black Lotus for 0 life with
# Bot2 unable to cast its own Bolt from exile meanwhile, then the Bolt at Bot2 for 1 life and Looting for 1 life, an untapped
# Mountain notwithstanding. Bot1 controlled those spells and that Lotus, so when they go to Bot2's graveyard they stay there.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus x3
Valgavoth, Terror Eater
Swamp x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Black Lotus
Faithless Looting
Lightning Bolt
Plains x3
